{"id":"u-04e8c9d1-d4fe-488b-a2d0-cbded22c55a0","src":"community","title":"Maximum","author":"Maxime-Terrence M.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/1WvKPt-maximuscle-powerlifting","desc":"Based on the Maximuscle Powerlifting Program, I added my own twist to it with a few added weeks and deload. \n\nThe Main lifts are trained for strength, with two other compound lifts used as accessories (Military press and Bent Rows).  \n\nDo this program on a caloric surplus of 150-500cal or recomp.  Make sure to eat about (0.8-1.1 x your BW) amount of protein. \n\nProperly warm up with dynamic movements before a workout and finish off with static stretches, no point of doing this workout if your body is wrecked. \n\nThis program is optimized for strength training, do not expect much hypertrophic gain from running this without additional accessories.  However, do be careful if you do so to prevent any neurological fatigue and/or injury.","level":["Intermediate"],"goals":["Strength"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":70,"joins":0,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-05-04T03:48:11.828Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Bench Press","Squat Day","Deadlift Day","Accessories"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":5,"pct":72.5,"x":5}],"note":"Ensure the bench bar touches your chest before pressing."},{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":6,"rpe":8,"x":3}],"note":"Pick a weight that feels heavy but comfortable."},{"n":"Pull-Up (Bodyweight)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":7,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Squat (Low Bar)","sets":[{"r":5,"pct":72.5,"x":5}],"note":"Make sure you hit ‘depth’ – which in powerlifting is the crease of your hip going lower than your knee."},{"n":"Front Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":8,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":8,"x":3}],"note":"60% of squat 1RM"},{"n":"Lying Leg Curl","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":7,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":5,"pct":72.5,"x":5}]},{"n":"Squat (Paused)","sets":[{"r":8,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":8,"